title: Microsoft Hyper-V VM: Network adapter
agents: windows
catalog: os/networking
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors a network adapter of a virtual machine running on
 Microsoft Hyper-V. It shows the name, the connection state, whether the MAC
 address is dynamic, the virtual switch and the VLAN mode and ID of the adapter.

 By default the check is {WARN} if the adapter is not connected. The rule
 "Hyper-V VM network adapter" configures the expected connection state, the
 expected MAC configuration and the expected virtual switch, and the state if
 they do not match. By default a static MAC address or any virtual switch is
 {OK}.

 The check is {WARN} if the VLAN mode or ID is missing and {UNKNOWN} if
 the connection state, the MAC configuration or the virtual switch is missing
 while it is checked.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_host.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V". The plug-in sends the data
 as piggyback data to a host with the name of the VM.

item:
 The GUID of the network adapter, which is the last part of its ID.

discovery:
 One service is created for each network adapter that reports a connection
 state.
